---
layout: changelog
title: Automatic image cropping with gravity=auto
date: 2026-09-10
cover: /images/blog/introducing-autogravity/cover.avif
tags: storage
---

The file preview endpoint now accepts `gravity=auto`. Instead of cropping toward a fixed position such as `center` or `top-left`, Appwrite finds the main subject of the image and keeps it in view.

```http
?width=400&height=400&gravity=auto
```

Automatic gravity is powered by [AutoGravity](https://github.com/appwrite/autogravity), an open-source Go service that returns a normalized focal point for an image. It checks for a confident face first using the YuNet detector, then falls back to U²-Net saliency detection to locate the strongest visual subject. AutoGravity never stores or modifies the image and does not perform face recognition.

Existing gravity values are unchanged. Automatic cropping only runs when a request sets `gravity` to `auto`, and transformed previews are cached as before.

Automatic gravity is available today on Appwrite Cloud and self-hosted support will arrive in the near future.

